Calculate the current S&P 500's 50-day moving average (DMA) and compare it to the 200-day moving average. If the 50-DMA has crossed above the 200-DMA (a "golden cross"), assign a bullish sentiment. Conversely, if the 50-DMA has crossed below the 200-DMA (a "death cross"), assign a bearish sentiment. Temper the conviction based on the volume of shares traded during the crossover event. If the volume was high, increase the conviction. Also, make a small positive bump to conviction if it's very early in the week and your strategy recommends.